verify sched_setaffinity intersect with cpuset controller works as expected.

The test will create cgroup with cpuset controler enabled, and run the syscall
within the cpuset controller, and check the return value, errno, and cpumask in
/proc/[pid]/status.

1. return -1 and errno EINVAL when the sched_setaffinity(cpumask is all zero)
2. return -1 and errno EINVAL when the sched_setaffinity(cpumask) cpu is all
   beyond the cpuset controller. the cpumask in status file keep unchanged
   as cpuset cpus.
3. return 0 when the sched_setaffinity (cpumask) cpu is partially in the cpuset
   controller. the cpumask is (cpuset cpu & sched_setaffinity cpu).
4. return 0 when the sched_setaffinity (cpumask) cpu is subset in the cpuset
   controller. the cpumask is (cpuset cpu & sched_setaffinity cpu).
